# Git Attributes for CI

# Pin the end-of-line form of every file in the repository so that the
# on-disk working tree and the committed blob are byte-identical under any
# client `core.autocrlf` setting. The CI matrix spans ubuntu-latest and
# windows-latest; Windows checkouts default to `core.autocrlf=true` and
# otherwise rewrite LF -> CRLF on disk. That rewrite silently breaks the
# prose gate in test/docs-facts.test.js, which keys on `## heading\n` and
# `^## N.` with a literal LF; a CRLF checkout makes both patterns fail and
# the suite goes red on Windows only (CI runs 36299141909 / 36299141870).
#
# `text eol=lf` forces LF on both checkout and commit for every text file,
# so a Windows client that has `core.autocrlf=true` globally still receives
# LF bytes on disk. This is the standard "repository declares LF" pattern.
#
# This file itself is text: it round-trips through the same rule, so adding
# or removing it cannot reintroduce the CRLF checkout it guards against.

# Everything is normalised to LF; no source file in this repository is
# committed with CRLF, so the blanket rule is safe and future-proof.
* text eol=lf

# The two binary families that do NOT survive a line-ending rewrite.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.exe binary
*.wasm binary
